<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Privilegium Minus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1156</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Privilegium Minus was a charter issued by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> in 1156 that raised the Margraviate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> to a duchy. It compensated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-austria">Henry II Jasomirgott</a> of the Babenberg family for giving up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, and granted the new duchy unusual rights, including inheritance through daughters and limited military obligations to the empire, laying the basis of Austria's later status.</p></div>
